{"ts":1793398257712,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103 shipped. validateApp (libs/shared-contracts, now 2.0.0) rejects apps without a non-empty owner. All three callers now pass owner: core-shell -> 'platform', billing -> 'payments', reports -> 'insights'. PRs #1 (contract), #2 (billing), #3 (core-shell), #4 (reports), all CI green and merged; CI/CD on main green after each. Assumptions: (1) shared-contracts is inlined at build time, so 'release' = merge + major version bump in package.json, nothing published to the registry; (2) owner values are hardcoded in each app because the build helper cannot read package.json, and they match each package.json team field; (3) reports was not in the ticket. It is not built or deployed by CD (CD only watches core-shell and billing), so its change is merged but not live; the CD SUCCESS on PR #4 does not mean reports was deployed; (4) apps were smoke-tested locally by evaluating the built bundles, not in a browser."}
